sub:assertion {
<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/agent/delphisci-resolvability-assessor-grok-4.7-high-fast> a prov:SoftwareAgent;
    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "delphisci dataset-resolvability assessor (Grok 4.7)";
    prov:actedOnBehalfOf <https://orcid.org/0009-0007-4948-9192>;
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/usesModel> <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/grok-4.7-high-fast>.
<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/grok-4.7-high-fast> a <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/LanguageModel>;
    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Grok 4.7";
    dc:identifier "grok-4.7-high-fast".
<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/darwin1859-ch06-08--grok> a <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/LLMClaimAssessment>;
    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Grok 4.7 on darwin1859-ch06-08: not-empirically-resolvable, resolvability 0.12";
    dc:description "The empirical clause that no such organ is known reports a state of argument rather than a measurable frequency. Any organ still lacking a known intermediate is compatible with the rule, because the rule demands a demonstration of impossibility, which comparative and fossil data cannot supply. Scores stay near the floor because there is no decision criterion a dataset could meet.";
    dc:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/dataset-resolvability-0.1.0>;
    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Proposed test with existing data: The sentence is a falsification rule: the theory fails if some complex organ could not possibly have been reached by successive slight modifications. No measurement records impossibility of every pathway, and a gap in known intermediates does not decide it.";
    prov:wasAttributedTo <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/agent/delphisci-resolvability-assessor-grok-4.7-high-fast>;
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/assessmentType> "dataset-resolvability/0.1.0";
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/evidenceAgainst> "Impossibility of every gradual pathway is modal, not a dataset variable.", "Missing intermediates are predicted both by true saltation and by an incomplete record, so the outcomes do not discriminate.";
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/hasConfidence> "0.74"^^xsd:double;
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/hasScore> "0.118"^^xsd:double;
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/hasVerdict> "not-empirically-resolvable".
<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/darwin1859-ch06-08--grok--analysis-feasibility> a <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/LLMClaimAssessment>;
    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Analysis feasibility of darwin1859-ch06-08 by Grok 4.7: 0.12";
    dc:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/dataset-resolvability-0.1.0-analysis-feasibility>;
    prov:wasAttributedTo <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/agent/delphisci-resolvability-assessor-grok-4.7-high-fast>;
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/assessmentType> "dataset-resolvability/0.1.0/analysis-feasibility";
